    end_line: 57
    content: "# Google Sheets API\n\n## Scopes\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and delete all\n    of your Google Drive files.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and delete\n    only the specific Google Drive files you use with this app.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly` \342\200\224 See and download all your\n    Google Drive files.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and\n    delete all your Google Sheets spreadsheets.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets.readonly` \342\200\224 See all your\n    Google Sheets spreadsheets.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n-   **Spreadsheets**: The file container for sheets.\n-   **Sheets**: Individual tabs within a spreadsheet.\n-   **Ranges**: A specific set of cells (e.g., \"Sheet1!A1:B10\").\n-   **Values**: The data contained within cells.\n-   **BatchUpdate**: Perform multiple updates (formatting, structure) at once.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n-   **Avoid hardcoding sheet names**: Never assume the first sheet is named\n    \"Sheet1\". Always fetch spreadsheet metadata first to identify the actual tab\n    names, or allow the user to select the sheet.\n\n## Client-Side Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Read range\nconst res = await fetch(`https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/${spreadsheetId}/values/${range}`, {\n  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n});\n```\n\n## Server-Side Pattern (Next.js API Route)\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/sheets/route.ts\nexport async function GET(req: NextRequest) {\n  const token = req.headers.get(\'Authorization\');\n  const { searchParams } = new URL(req.url);\n  const spreadsheetId = searchParams.get(\'spreadsheetId\');\n  const range = searchParams.get(\'range\');\n  const res = await fetch(`https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/${spreadsheetId}/values/${range}`, {\n    headers: { Authorization: token! },\n  });\n  return NextResponse.json(await res.json());\n}\n```\n"
    raw_content: "# Google Sheets API\n\n## Scopes\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and delete all\n    of your Google Drive files.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and delete\n    only the specific Google Drive files you use with this app.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly` \342\200\224 See and download all your\n    Google Drive files.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and\n    delete all your Google Sheets spreadsheets.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets.readonly` \342\200\224 See all your\n    Google Sheets spreadsheets.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n-   **Spreadsheets**: The file container for sheets.\n-   **Sheets**: Individual tabs within a spreadsheet.\n-   **Ranges**: A specific set of cells (e.g., \"Sheet1!A1:B10\").\n-   **Values**: The data contained within cells.\n-   **BatchUpdate**: Perform multiple updates (formatting, structure) at once.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n-   **Avoid hardcoding sheet names**: Never assume the first sheet is named\n    \"Sheet1\". Always fetch spreadsheet metadata first to identify the actual tab\n    names, or allow the user to select the sheet.\n\n## Client-Side Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Read range\nconst res = await fetch(`https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/${spreadsheetId}/values/${range}`, {\n  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n});\n```\n\n## Server-Side Pattern (Next.js API Route)\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/sheets/route.ts\nexport async function GET(req: NextRequest) {\n  const token = req.headers.get(\'Authorization\');\n  const { searchParams } = new URL(req.url);\n  const spreadsheetId = searchParams.get(\'spreadsheetId\');\n  const range = searchParams.get(\'range\');\n  const res = await fetch(`https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/${spreadsheetId}/values/${range}`, {\n    headers: { Authorization: token! },\n  });\n  return NextResponse.json(await res.json());\n}\n```\n"
    num_lines: 58
    num_bytes: 1954
  }
}
