  planner_response {
    response: "Pour concevoir une interface de gestion de stock parfaitement adapt\303\251e \303\240 vos besoins op\303\251rationnels et \303\240 l\'int\303\251gration Google Sheets, voici quelques pr\303\251cisions cl\303\251s pour orienter le design et les flux de travail :"
    thinking: "**Reviewing Planning Mode**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the planning mode instructions and guidelines, specifically the initial interactive clarification and interview phase. I\'m carefully examining the prompt metadata triggers for plan or design requests. I want to ensure my understanding is robust and ready for implementation.\n\n\n**Refining Question Strategy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of the clarifying question process. My goal is to craft targeted multiple-choice inquiries, ensuring each option remains concise and easily understood. I\'m focusing on avoiding immediate plan generation, as I understand this bypasses the question UI. I\'ll yield immediately after asking questions to allow for user interaction. I\'m also ensuring to keep the chat response minimal.\n\n\n**Optimizing Question Design**\n\nI\'m now revising my question design strategy to align with expert guidance. I\'m prioritizing brevity and clarity in my questions, keeping them to one or two sentences. Option labels are being crafted to be concise and button-like, aiming for under ten words. I\'m structuring options between two and six per question, and avoiding the \"Other\" option. I\'m leading the options with any recommendations.\n\n\n**Adapting UI Approach**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interface preferences, framing questions around visual aesthetics and Google Sheets interaction. I\'m exploring three multiple-choice questions in French to maintain a seamless user experience. The first question explores visual orientation with three distinct options. The second prioritizes Google Sheets integration, again offering three options, including real-time synchronization. I\'m ensuring all options are concise.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Sector Questions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the first French questions to better understand the user\'s focus. I\'m starting with questions about the business sector to understand inventory type, and I\'m ensuring all options are clear, concise, and professional. I\'ve designed multiple-choice prompts to gather core context on the stock or sector. I prioritize the first question as a key starting point for any user requesting a plan.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_228727"
      name: "ask_question"
      arguments_json: "{\"questions\":[{\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Commerce de d\303\251tail et boutique multi-produits\", \"Entrep\303\264t industriel et pi\303\250ces techniques\", \"Restauration et produits avec dates de p\303\251remption\", \"Mat\303\251riel d\'entreprise et parc informatique\"], \"question\":\"Quel est le secteur d\'activit\303\251 ou le type de stock \303\240 g\303\251rer ?\"}, {\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Interface claire et nette avec touches bleues professionnelles\", \"Th\303\250me sombre technique pour op\303\251rateur logistique\", \"Style minimaliste noir et blanc avec forte lisibilit\303\251\"], \"question\":\"Quelle direction visuelle et ambiance pr\303\251f\303\251rez-vous pour le tableau de bord ?\"}, {\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Synchronisation bidirectionnelle directe et journal des mouvements\", \"Consultation analytique et alertes de seuil critique\", \"Importation initiale et export ponctuel de rapports\"], \"question\":\"Quelle priorit\303\251 souhaitez-vous pour le flux avec Google Sheets ?\"}], \"toolAction\":\"Asking design preferences\", \"toolSummary\":\"Stock management design questionnaire\"}"
