  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Architectural Needs**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on defining the core architecture for StockFlow. I\'ve begun outlining the essential data structures within `src/types.ts`. The `Product` type encompasses details like ID, SKU, name, category, quantity, cost and sale prices, and supplier. I\'ve also defined the `StockMovement` type to represent inventory transactions. This includes details about products moved in and out of the system.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the data models, expanding the `StockMovement` type to cover various reasons for inventory changes, including standard French reasons. I\'m also adding `Category` type for product categories and `SheetsSyncStatus` to track Google Sheets synchronization. Finally, I\'ve defined `FilterOptions` for flexible data display.\n\n\n**Implementing Google Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the Google Sheets integration. I\'m building functions like `googleSignIn()`, `getAccessToken()`, and `logout()` within a component, and I\'ve started on a styled Google sign-in button. I\'m creating a `src/services/googleSheets.ts` service with key functions, including `syncToSheets()` and `readFromSheets()`. I\'m also preparing a `createNewSpreadsheet()` function and defining the expected tab structure with specific column headings for both \"Produits\" and \"Mouvements\" tabs.\n\n\n**Developing Initial Data**\n\nI\'ve just added initial product data and stock movement logs to `src/data/initialProducts.ts`. The inventory items cover clothing, tech, home goods, beauty, and gourmet food, with realistic SKUs, quantities, prices, and suppliers. I\'m also preparing the application state within `src/context/StockContext.tsx`.\n\nI\'m focused on setting up handlers for all core features, including `recordMovement`, `addProduct`, `updateProduct`, `deleteProduct`, and `bulkImport`. These will update the inventory, and track the user\'s modifications through localStorage, and syncing data with Google Sheets.\n\n\n**Designing UI Framework**\n\nI\'m currently creating the UI components, ensuring they strictly follow the \"frontend-design\" guidelines. I\'m focusing on the \"Zero-Pill Rule\" for informational metadata, using clean, unboxed text with subtle typographic separators. I\'m also using `tabular-nums font-mono` for all numeric values and date displays. I\'m now structuring the SaaS workspace canvas, including the sidebar, top bar, and views. I plan to incorporate both automatic and manual sync triggers.\n\n\n**Structuring Dashboard Data**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the dashboard view, aiming for concise and actionable information. I\'m prioritizing key elements like a mini-table for urgent re-stock alerts, and the latest stock movements. I also have plans for a category-based visual, and aim to include actionable buttons. I\'ve also implemented the inventory table, and movement ledger.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_219379"
      name: "view_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"AbsolutePath\":\"/firebase-applet-config.json\", \"toolAction\":\"Viewing firebase-applet-config.json\", \"toolSummary\":\"Check Firebase configuration\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
