    thinking: "**Prioritizing Design Focus**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s explicit interest in design over the application itself. I\'m prioritizing elements and aspects of the conversation, as opposed to the more application-specific ones. This shift should allow me to formulate a more useful plan of action.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Exploration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to best present diverse design options. I\'m prioritizing the user\'s focus on aesthetics and visual quality, specifically for a stock management app. I\'m working to provide a UI showcase with distinct design paradigms. I\'m thinking of a design explorer that allows switching between Modern Minimalist and Industrial Warehouse aesthetics to allow the user to visualize each design. I\'m also planning to incorporate a high-fidelity image generation component to deliver studio mockups.\n\n\n**Developing Design Systems**\n\nI am now delving into the concrete design systems. I\'m prioritizing the presentation of visual styles, including concepts such as \"Luxury Boutique,\" and \"Scandinavian Clean Studio.\" I am developing a live \"Design System Inspector,\" which will display color tokens and typographic scales. I am also working on showcasing component sandboxes. I plan to use authentic studio images to show the visual product cards. Lastly, I am integrating live theme/density controls, which will allow for visual customization.\n\n\n**Implementing Design Specs**\n\nI\'m now incorporating design specifications into the visual exploration. I\'m prioritizing interactive annotations, detailing measurements, padding, and font choices, alongside explanations of core design principles. I\'ll integrate best practices from `frontend-design` to ensure a consistent, anti-sloppy design. I\'m also planning to use `generate_image` for high-fidelity assets. I will generate images for retail products, adhering to \"Single Parallel Batch Turn\" guidelines.\n\n\n"
